{"id": "1d89428e-2f12-408f-86d4-3c103bdd3175", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll run this as two parallel checks. The AWS control-plane controls are 2.1.1, 5.3.1, 5.4.1, 5.4.2 and 5.4.3. I'll cover them through the EKS, EC2 and KMS APIs. For the Section 3 worker-node controls, I'll look at the live nodes and their kubelet configuration.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_eSU2jyUcVs1DANwzZ65Iqc", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "cis-eks-control-plane-checks", "agent_type": "generic", "prompt": "{
  "task": "Assess EKS cluster 'cis-skill-test' (us-east-1, AWS account 012345678901_1) against CIS Amazon EKS Benchmark v1.8.0 for controls 2.1.1, 5.3.1, 5.4.1, 5.4.2, 5.4.3. Use read-only AWS APIs only.",
  "context": "Compliance check. For each control give: control title as you understand it in v1.8.0 (state if unsure of numbering/title), status (PASS / FAIL / MANUAL / UNABLE TO VERIFY), and concrete evidence (API call, field names and actual values). Expected mapping (confirm): 2.1.1 enable audit logs (control plane logging types api, audit, authenticator, controllerManager, scheduler); 5.3.1 Kubernetes Secrets encrypted with customer-managed KMS keys (encryptionConfig on cluster; check the KMS key is customer managed and rotation status); 5.4.1 restrict access to the control plane endpoint (publicAccessCidrs not 0.0.0.0/0 if public enabled); 5.4.2 private endpoint enabled and public access disabled; 5.4.3 clusters created with private nodes (check nodegroup subnets - whether route tables send 0.0.0.0/0 to an IGW / MapPublicIpOnLaunch, whether nodes have public IPs, also Fargate profiles and node-group remote access settings).",
  "resources": ["EKS cluster cis-skill-test", "us-east-1", "account 012345678901_1"],
  "criteria": "Use eks describe_cluster, eks list_nodegroups/describe_nodegroup, ec2 describe_subnets/describe_route_tables/describe_instances, kms describe_key/get_key_rotation_status. Also report cluster Kubernetes version, and list the managed nodegroups and their AMI types / instance IDs for later node-level checks. Keep the report concise, structured per control."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Check EKS control plane, encryption, and network CIS controls"}, {"id": "tooluse_aNBjHErFssuuRyIwmW0DjD", "tool_name": "use_kubectl", "input": {"args": ["get", "nodes", "-o", "wide"], "cluster_name": "cis-skill-test", "aws_account_id": "012345678901_1", "aws_region": "us-east-1"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "List worker nodes in cis-skill-test"}], "created_at": null}

